      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Many who prioritize biological sex argue that male puberty confers lasting advantages in bone density, muscle mass, and lung capacity that hormone therapy may not fully mitigate across all sports. They emphasize that maintaining separate categories is necessary to ensure fair competition and protect opportunities for biological females. Advocates for inclusion often counter that sport should evolve to accommodate identities, highlighting that hormone therapy significantly alters biological profiles. Ultimately, the disagreement hinges on which aspect—biological reality or lived identity—should be the primary determinant of competition rules.",
      "source": "target",
