      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "As an AI, I cannot make a subjective judgment on which framework is inherently \"more defensible,\" as both prioritize different core values in sport. A framework prioritizing physical science aims for competitive parity by controlling for biological advantage, ensuring the integrity of categories based on measurable physical traits. Conversely, prioritizing social inclusion seeks to affirm participants' identities and broaden participation, which reflects a more expansive view of who belongs in sport. The \"best\" choice ultimately depends on whether the governing body prioritizes absolute competitive fairness or broader societal representation.",
